{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For YHWH will judge His people, etc.</b> After He finished the matter of those who provoke El to their end, He returned to promise the totality of Israel that He will not contend with them forever. ״כִּי יָדִין ה׳ עַמּוֹ״ — meaning, He will set up in judgment the cups of reeling that they [the nations] made them pass through, and He will see the troubles that passed over the righteous — some of them they killed, some of them they burned, some of them they flayed — and on account of the righteous who suffered He will be consoled. This is what He said: ״וְעַל עֲבָדָיו יִתְנֶחָם״ — meaning, for their sake He will be consoled to say, ״enough of the troubles of exile.״ Further, when YHWH sees that there is no strength in Israel to save themselves from exile, and there is no strength in the righteous to chastise with the rod of reproof those who provoke El, and there will no longer remain in Israel great men and prophets, seers, possessors of the holy spirit, and ״אֵין אֶשְׁכּוֹל״ etc. (Micah 7:1) — this is what He said: ״כִּי אָזְלַת יָד״, and in this ״אֶפֶס עָצוּר״ — meaning, after the manner of (I Samuel 9:17) ״יַעְצֹר בְּעַמִּי״ — meaning, that there is no strength in those who guide in the ways of HaShem to guide them; ״וְעָזוּב״ — meaning, and from this side the people remains forsaken."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:40.048254259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}